---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import InteriorHero from '../../components/InteriorHero.astro';
import SectionShell from '../../components/SectionShell.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Commercial Epoxy Flooring Edmonton | Final Finish" description="Plan commercial epoxy flooring in Edmonton around traffic, concrete condition, cleaning and staged downtime before choosing a finish." canonicalPath="/services/commercial-epoxy-flooring">
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content">
    <InteriorHero eyebrow="Warehouses · Showrooms · Industrial" title="Commercial floors that present the space clearly." lead="Commercial flooring planning begins with how people, products, water and cleaning move through the space—not a generic coating claim." />
    <SectionShell>
      <p class="section-kicker">Map the operation</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Plan around traffic before selecting texture</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Walk the space with the people who use and clean it. Mark entrances, aisles, turning routes, loading areas, drains, fixed equipment, thresholds and zones that must remain available. Then describe footwear, carts or wheeled loads, spills, water, grit, cleaners and any direct light that affects the finish choice.</p>
      <p>Texture and cleanability need to be discussed together. A finish is not universally slip-proof, and a coarse surface that cannot be cleaned with the planned method can create another operational problem. The <a href="/resources/slip-resistance-floor-coatings">slip-resistance planning guide</a> and <a href="/resources/warehouse-floor-coating-planning">warehouse planning guide</a> provide questions that keep use conditions visible.</p>
    </SectionShell>
    <SectionShell tone="stone">
      <p class="section-kicker">Before work starts</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Make downtime a written operating plan</h2>
      <p>Application is only one part of the interruption. A workable plan identifies access, clearing and protection of inventory or equipment, preparation, repairs, each layer, inspection, permitted reopening activities and who approves changes if conditions differ from the assumptions. It should distinguish pedestrian access from rolling loads, cleaning, equipment placement and normal operations according to the documented system restrictions.</p>
      <p>Use the <a href="/resources/commercial-flooring-downtime-planning">commercial downtime plan</a> to separate these stages. For a showroom or retail setting, the <a href="/resources/retail-flooring-coating-planning">retail planning guide</a> adds questions about display changes, customer routes and cleaning equipment. Site-specific safety, occupancy and accessibility controls remain the responsibility of the relevant workplace and building parties.</p>
    </SectionShell>
    <SectionShell>
      <p class="section-kicker">Scope and substrate</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">The slab, not the brochure, determines the preparation conversation</h2>
      <p>Record cracks, joints, spalls, old coatings, adhesive, oil, moisture indicators and areas hidden beneath fixtures. A condition found after clearing or mechanical preparation may change repairs, sequencing or cost; the proposal should state how it will be documented and authorized. Where moisture is relevant, request the test method, locations, results and the proposed system’s current limits rather than accepting a general moisture-barrier claim.</p>
      <p>Bring the <a href="/resources/concrete-moisture-testing-floor-coatings">moisture-testing guide</a> and <a href="/resources/concrete-cracks-spalling-floor-coating">concrete-condition guide</a> into the review. The <a href="/resources/questions-to-ask-floor-coating-contractor">contractor question list</a> helps keep materials, preparation, return-to-service and maintenance records comparable across quotes.</p>
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/contact#quote">Discuss a commercial floor</a>
    </SectionShell>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
